ent the Downing Street Rose Garden  is usually reserved for foreign leaders  not back from a slate but this week that  changed no I don't I don't regret what I  did as I said I think reasonable people  may well disagree and the smile on his  face at the end suggested mr. Cummings  believed he got his way someone would  say oh no DOM is against that Dom  doesn't want this Dom says no to that  and that was effectively the closing  down of any discussion if it was felt  that Dominic coming somehow mind was set  against a particular course of action  there was almost no point in continuing  to argue for anything different there  was speculation when Dominic Cummings  first arrived here that he wouldn't hang  around for long but this saga has made  it abundantly clear Boris Johnson  believes mr. Cummings is just as  critical for he wants to achieve in  power as he was getting him into it the  evidence of history points very clearly  and without any equivocation to the fact  that when the aide to the Prime Minister  the  a big story themselves almost as  dominant as the Prime Minister they  cannot stay because it breaks apart  everything in our democratic  constitution for now Boris Johnson's  chief adviser is protected the comings  crisis is put to rest but with huge  challenges ahead there may well be  another on the horizon Joe Pike Sky News  Westminster
 

